+   - The histogram strip.
+   - The number of chart rows and the dots per row: the band and the median only on compact phones, the outliers as a count.
+   - The "›N" chips, the with/without-pay line, and Clusters/Ranges plus the grouping (one control at compact sizes?).
+   - The header's pills.
+   - The sheet's peek height, so that at least one full job card shows on the first screen at every phone size.
+   Bigger screens (Pro Max, Fold open, Duo spanned, iPad) earn more, up to the desktop layout. Give each rule a measurable check, e.g. "at 375x625, a card's title and pay are above the fold, and at most N text lines sit above the first card", so fix-ui-6 can turn each into an e2e test. Keep the UI simple and in plain words: no new visible control unless it replaces two.
